  "raw_text": "probably usually go with either chicken strips or chicken sandwich. The chicken sandwich I prefer if it has some vegetables such as tomato and lettuce. So honestly, for chicken sandwich, I think a McChicken I prefer over a over Chick-fil-A because Chick-fil-A doesn't have any vegetables and stuff. It's just kind of like a plain chicken piece and then maybe a pickle. In terms of my chicken strips, to be honest, I don't know if fast food restaurants have that amazing chicken strips. Chicken strips, honestly, is more something I get from the hot food aisle of a grocery store or even a cafeteria or like, yeah, something like that, I think. Although, I mean, Popeye's has good chicken strips, I think. Is it Popeye's? It might be Popeye's. Agent: Thank you for those examples, William. So you mentioned the McDonald's McChicken, Chick-fil-A's chicken sandwich, and chicken strips, possibly from Popeye's or a grocery store. Could you elaborate on what's better or worse about these items compared",
